      sources: "Sources: examples/privileged-access fixtures (fictional tenant). Chapter 01, “Lab 1: fixtures, no tenant,” steps 4–6 and the expected result.",
      say: `Reading the findings is where the rules become real. Seven rows are standing privilege in the top tiers, including a service principal whose exception nobody owns, so the exception doesn't count. One Global Administrator also elevated to root. There are five Global Administrators once the group's members are counted, and five owners on one subscription. The emergency account is only informational, because it's a listed exception with an owner. Then you watch the reader refuse an undeclared call and an unknown cloud. The whole suite passes, three hundred thirty tests.`,
      detail: `Step 4, read the findings: Get-Content out/inventory/findings.json -Raw | ConvertFrom-Json | Where-Object Severity -eq 'Finding' | Format-Table Rule, Object. Seven PA-INV-01 rows (a standing Global Administrator, the mail automation service principal whose exception has no owner, two standing subscription Owners, a standing User Access Administrator at the management group, the same Global Administrator's User Access Administrator at root, and a log-export service principal with standing Contributor on the control-plane subscription), PA-INV-07 for the root-scope elevation, PA-INV-04 (five Global Administrators, one of them through PRV-T0-GlobalAdmin), and PA-INV-08 (five Owners on the workload subscription). Azure rows show object IDs, because Resource Manager returns IDs, not names. The emergency account ea01 is Info, not a Finding: it's on the exceptions list with an owner. Step 5, see the reader refuse: $r = New-PaReader -Cloud gcc -Task inventory -Invoke (New-PaFixtureInvoker -Path tests/fixtures/tenant.json).Invoke; Invoke-PaList -Reader $r -CallId ca-policies; Get-PaCloud GCCHigh. Two errors: "Undeclared call 'ca-policies' for task 'inventory'; add it to config/calls.json with its permission." and "Unknown cloud 'GCCHigh'. Use global, gcc, gcchigh or dod." Step 6, run the tests: Invoke-Pester -Path tests. Expected result: 330 tests passing, every row of the gap table seen with your own eyes, and out/inventory/manifest.json listing 24 GET requests. Delete out when you're done.`,
