      sources: "Sources: Learn, List Microsoft Entra role assignments (Download assignments). Chapter 01, “Lab 2: test tenant.”",
      say: `Lab 2 moves to a test tenant with fictional people, never production, and it only reads. You register the app in the tenant's own cloud with a certificate, grant exactly the five permissions plus Reader on a test subscription, sign in, and run. Then comes the useful part: download the admin center's list of assignments, as Learn describes, and compare. Every active row should be in the inventory, and the inventory should also hold the eligible rows the download can't see. Check the two assumptions the fixture made, then back everything out.`,
      detail: `Use a test tenant in the worldwide or GCC cloud with a test Azure subscription, never production, with fictional people. The run only reads. 1 Register the app in the tenant's own cloud. For a GCC tenant that's the worldwide Microsoft Entra admin center. Add a certificate credential, not a secret. 2 Grant the five application permissions from Lab 1, step 2, and grant admin consent. Nothing else. 3 Grant Reader to the app's service principal on the test subscription. 4 Sign in and run: Connect-MgGraph -Environment Global -TenantId <tenant-id> -ClientId <app-id> -CertificateThumbprint <thumbprint>; Connect-AzAccount -ServicePrincipal -Environment AzureCloud -Tenant <tenant-id> -ApplicationId <app-id> -CertificateThumbprint <thumbprint>; ./Invoke-PaInventory.ps1 -Cloud gcc -OutputPath out/inventory-test -AzureScope /subscriptions/<test-subscription-id> -TenantId <tenant-id>. 5 Cross-check against the admin center: on Roles and administrators, select Download assignments for all roles, as Learn's procedure describes. Every active row in the CSV should be in inventory.csv, and inventory.csv should hold the eligible rows the CSV doesn't. 6 Check the two things the fixture assumed: open inventory.json and confirm that rows read with $expand=principal have a principal type (research gaps, row 2), and that each Azure schedule appears once. 7 Back it out: remove the Reader assignment and the five permissions, delete the app registration and its certificate, and delete out/inventory-test: it holds the tenant's privileged holders.`,
